[Unit]
Description=Forge daily learned-verdict-model train + eval (F3 criterion clock)
Documentation=file://%h/proj/Forge/scripts/daily_ranker_eval.sh

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=%h/proj/Forge
# D331 Part B (prereg 812d65bfbe86) — scope the F3/tail TRAINING POPULATION to
# honestly-evaluated rows. Crucible's stage-one screen structurally cannot produce
# an honest-coverage component, so 90.3% of the frame was labelled negative
# regardless of quality. ON => 364,545 rows/5.388% prevalence -> 35,320/55.609%,
# with the same 19,641 positives. Estimand shifts to P(component | honestly
# evaluated). Set HERE and not in forge.service: `build_dataset` is called only by
# the `ranker-model` CLI this unit runs, so the flag in the daemon unit would be a
# silent no-op (the shipped != deployed class, D330).
# ⚠️ TURNED OFF 2026-07-25 (Q59). The DROP is a COLLIDER, and that outweighs the
# estimand argument above. `honest_regime_coverage_row` is quality-correlated, so
# dropping on it biases every coefficient correlated with coverage-resolution --
# measured: 9 of 81 sign-FLIP. Worse, it deletes whole strata: rank_k=20 has 55,820
# rows unconditioned and ZERO under the drop, so the model could not learn that k=20
# converts at 0% (D004 breadth floor) at any encoding.
# VALIDATED OUT OF SAMPLE, temporal split, judged on the unconditioned population:
#   robustness  OOS rank-IC   0.0321 (drop) -> 0.3962 (no-drop)     12x
#   F3          OOS AUC       0.5910 (drop) -> 0.6936 (no-drop + categorical rank_k)
# The live models were near coin-flip out of sample, found two independent ways.
# Ships TOGETHER with the categorical rank_k encoding in features.py -- arm F shows
# either alone is worthless or worse (drop+one-hot is byte-identical to drop+linear,
# because with k=20 deleted a one-hot over {5,10} IS a relabelled linear term).
# D331 Part B's cell-allocation benefit does NOT regress (arm E: unconditioned picks
# land marginally CLOSER to the ground-truth hypothesis mix).
# REVERT = set this back to `on` + retrain; the flag is read only by the ranker-model
# CLI this unit runs (a copy in forge.service would be a silent no-op, D330).
Environment=FORGE_HONEST_LABEL_SCOPE=off
ExecStart=%h/proj/Forge/scripts/daily_ranker_eval.sh
# Train on a ~10k-row frame is minutes of pure-Python IRLS; snapshot + eval add a
# little. Generous ceiling so a slow snapshot never wedges the timer.
TimeoutStartSec=30m
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
SyslogIdentifier=forge-ranker-eval
